[=#mysqlspecialpurpose]
= Special-Purpose Options =

== Mapping zero-scale DECIMAL to BIGINT ==

Some back-end databases (eg. Oracle) have no integer types, and store integers as DECIMALs with a scale of 0.  By default, the !MySQL protocol module reports these to the client as DECIMAL.  The //zeroscaledecimaltobigint// option makes it report them as BIGINT instead.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-mysqlfezeroscaledecimal.conf@
}}}
}}}

== Mapping DATE to DATETIME ==

Some back-end databases (eg. Oracle) have a single DATE type that can store both a date and a time.  By default, the !MySQL protocol module reports it to the client as DATE.  If the back-end returns times in DATE columns, the //datetodatetime// option makes the module report them as DATETIME instead.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-mysqlfedatetodatetime.conf@
}}}
}}}

== Supporting Older !MariaDB JDBC Drivers ==

Older !MariaDB JDBC drivers (eg. 1.4.6) throw a !NullPointerException when connecting.  The //oldmariadbjdbcservercapabilitieshack// option works around this.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-mysqlfeoldmariadbjdbc.conf@
}}}
}}}

